  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Gina Hinojosa, a member of the Democratic Party, has represented the 49th district in the Texas House of Representatives since 2017.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383859577:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "Before she became a state legislator, Hinojosa worked as a labor and civil rights lawyer.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383859577:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Regina Inez Hinojosa, born December 8, 1973, is an American politician and lawyer who is the governor-elect of Texas.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383859577:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Hinojosa was born on 8 December 1973 in McAllen.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q28314533:P569",
        "wd:Q28314533:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "She was educated at the University of Texas at Austin and at George Washington University Law School.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q28314533:P69:Q49213",
        "wd:Q28314533:P69:Q5546035"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:37Z",
      "text": "She has also worked in Austin.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q28314533:P937:Q16559"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:43Z",
      "text": "Readers also turned to the pages for Greg Abbott (327,943), Ken Paxton (197,914) and the 2026 Texas gubernatorial election (158,747).",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Greg_Abbott:2026-11-04",
        "views:en:Ken_Paxton:2026-11-04",
        "views:en:2026_Texas_gubernatorial_election:2026-11-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:52Z",
      "text": "On 4 November 2026, 1,242,354 people read about Hinojosa, about 195 times the usual level.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Gina_Hinojosa:2026-11-04",
        "views:en:Gina_Hinojosa:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:59Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 11 languages, and after English, Spanish had the most readers at 92,588.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Gina_Hinojosa:2026-11-04",
        "views:es:Gina_Hinojosa:2026-11-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:01:06Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers, and a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:es:Gina_Hinojosa:2026-11-04",
        "views:de:Gina_Hinojosa:2026-11-04",
